 ## Overview
-RefSR-NeRF is a framework that combines a standard NeRF backbone with a Reference-guided Super-Resolution CNN (RefSR-CNN) to synthesize high-quality novel views from low-resolution inputs [S2]. It solves the parameter explosion and memory constraints of training NeRF directly on high-resolution data by decoupling 3D field optimization from high-frequency detail reconstruction [S2]. Unlike methods that modify the NeRF architecture directly (e.g., [AdaNeRF](6195-adanerf.md)) or use generative priors (e.g., [DiffusioNeRF](8703-diffusionerf.md)), RefSR-NeRF preserves the standard radiance field while using a separate CNN to inject details guided by a single high-resolution reference image [S2].
